AcquisitionMethod: data-dependent mode
AlkylationReagent: iodoacetamide
CleavageAgent: Lys-C
CleavageAgent: trypsin
CollisionEnergy: normal collision energy of 28
Disease: high-grade serous ovarian cancer (HGSOC)
Disease: triple-negative breast cancer (TNBC)
EnrichmentMethod: ECM proteins were enriched from frozen whole tissue or tumor sections (20 x 30 mum sections, ~40-50 mg of tissue), as previously described.
FactorValue: triple-negative breast cancer
FactorValue: adjacent mammary tissue
FactorValue: omental metastasis from high-grade serous ovarian cancer
FactorValue: normal omentum
FlowRateChromatogram: 1 mL/min
FractionationMethod: Off-Line Fractionation of Peptides by Reversed-Phase Chromatography at High pH
FragmentMassTolerance: 15 mmu for fragment-ion mass tolerance
GradientTime: an 80 min gradient
GradientTime: The gradient conditions were 0-10% B (0-5 min), 10-30% B (5-105 min), 30-40% B (105-119 min), 40-60% B (119-124 min), 60-100% B (124-126 min), 100% B (126-136 min), 100-0% B (136-138 min), and 0% B (138-140 min)
Instrument: QExactive mass spectrometer (Thermo)
IonizationType: nanoelectrospray
MaterialType: tissue
Modification: carbamidomethylation of cysteine
Modification: oxidized methionine
Modification: deamidation of asparagine
Modification: pyro-glutamic acid modification at N-terminal glutamine
Modification: hydroxylation of lysine and proline
NumberOfBiologicalReplicates: 2
NumberOfFractions: 15
NumberOfMissedCleavages: two missed cleavages
Organism: Homo sapiens
OrganismPart: triple-negative breast cancer
OrganismPart: adjacent mammary tissue
OrganismPart: normal omentum
PrecursorMassTolerance: 10 ppm mass tolerance for precursor ions
ReductionReagent: dithiothreitol
Separation: reversed-phase HPLC using an EASY-nLC1000 (Thermo Scientific) using a pre-column (made in house, 6 cm of 10 mum C18) and a self-pack 5 mum tip analytical column (12 cm of 5 mum C18, New Objective)
Sex: women
Temperature : 37 degreesC